{"agent":"bg114","data":{"digest":"c79d2cc2854e0f89","finding":1,"gate":"rubber_duck","location":"tests/test_gate_run_after_merge.py:170","probe":"The finding misreads the test's command. `command = \"true\"` genuinely runs and exits 0, so the fresh gate run records `passed` the item EARNED -- it is not a stale partial kept over the measured evidence and not an `unavailable` erase (the B-merged-partial-records-unavailable defect this bug fixes). A command that actually failed would record its own failure the same way. The fix re-measures; it never fabricates a green: it reruns the command at merged_sha. The old 'baseline.red survives' assertion guarded the REMOVED no-tree path this fix replaces, not a re-measurement.","severity":"HIGH","title":"tests/test_gate_run_after_merge.py:170","verdict":"refuted"},"id":"e4e2c7f4d81a416c56a3e0c47","kind":"review.triaged","lamport":159038,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B80a4dafd02","ts":"2026-11-09T03:51:15.862359Z"}
